# Firestore Security Rules requirements

## Users
- A user can read their own user doc.
- A user can update ONLY safe profile fields (displayName, photoURL, countryId, cityId).
- `role` and `isActive` can only be changed by admin.

## Workshops
- Public read only if `status == "published"`.
- Teacher can create/update only if `teacherId == auth.uid`.
- Admin can read/write everything.

## Sessions
- Public read only if the parent workshop is published (or session is for a published workshop).
- Teacher can create/update sessions only for their own workshops.

## Enrollments
- Student can create enrollment only for themselves (`studentId == auth.uid`).
- Student can read only their enrollments.
- Teacher can read enrollments where `teacherId == auth.uid`.
- Admin full access.

## Payments
- Restrict reads to involved parties (student/teacher/admin).
- Prevent client from updating `payments.status`; only server/admin can update it.
- Later: allow backend webhook only (not client).

## Reviews/Favorites/Blog
- Favorites: user manages only their own.
- Reviews: ideally require paid enrollment for that workshop (TODO allowed initially, but must be tracked).
- Blog posts: public read only published; write only admin.

